    "summary": "A woman&#039;s skirt wrap, known as a &#039;katrinca&#039;.  Rectangular in shape, with a solid black centre [75 cm wide] bordered by predominantly brown panels.  Twill woven [2/2 twill] from wool, hand woven, with the selvedges worn at the waist and hem.  The two bordering panels [32 cm approx] have alternating brown wool and multicoloured wool and cotton stripes (woven as bands): green, pink, purple and black woollen thread and pink and orange cotton thread.  The warp ends are turned and hemmed.  Some small holes in the black centre field.  The red band (woven as a stripe) is the hem.",
